{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/29211-orpheus-story-arc","id":29211,"title":"Orpheus story arc","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-13T02:40:17-08:00","id":29211,"title":"Orpheus story arc","content":"I don't really know anything about the books, but from the wikipedia page on them it sounds interesting. What exactly was the story arc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1567-clockwork-chaos","name":"Clockwork Chaos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T04:54:36-08:00","id":29249,"title":"","content":"Well as you know the entire arc is told over the course of the line, each book adding new events. It's been a while since I've read the line but here's what I remember. The first book obviously sets up the universe, explaining the Orpheus Group and all that. The next one sees the Orpheus Group destroyed* by rival company NextWorld and the survivors forced into hiding while continuing their investigations into the Restless Dead. The third book sees the drug pigment, an early projection drug that's been turned into the street drug of choice, tainted with poison, killing hundreds, most notably at a huge rave. Worse the ghosts of those killed are used by spectres to create hives in the living world. I can't remember which of the two is next but one involves a chuck of Stygia being thrown out of the Underworld and into ours while the other sees the rise of the Orphan-Grinders, former spectres that have managed to return to who they were as well as the first book to really bring Grandmother, the ultimate evil of Orpheus and perhaps Oblivion itself, into the picture. The final book, End Game sees the return to the Underworld and what's happened to it since WtO ended and ultimately is about one thing and one thing only, stopping Grandmother no matter the cost.<br /> <br /> All and all it is a great line and sorely underrated in my opinion. I highly recommend picking it up, especially if you're a WtO and/or GtSE fan.<br /> <br /> EDIT:Forgot to add. *While the Orpheus Group collapsed the survivors built their own company from the ashes, Lazarus Redux.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","user":"AkatsukiLeader13","date":". 12-13-2013, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}